# rule.forbid.domain-term-inconsistency

one concept, one word, even before a canon exists. two or more words for the **same** concept with **no canonical term declared** is forbidden. pre-canon twin of `rule.forbid.domain-term-synonyms`.

test: *is this concept named the same way everywhere?* two or more words → confirm truly one concept, coin the canonical word (`howto.domain-term-disputes` if arguable), itemize it (`rule.require.domain-term-itemization`), conform the rest or leave until disturbed.

blocker: one concept named with two or more words across contracts, no canonical term declared.
